PS5 Pro: upstream #66 (Borchev), ported to 7.3

ps5-linux-patches 53809a3 "PS5 Pro fixes, add GPU governor", on top of our #58 port:
 - GPU clock governor: drivers/ps5/gpufreq.c (devfreq, 500-2350 MHz on the Pro, 500-2230 MHz
   on the base PS5) with a thermal limit, 85 C by default (ps5_gpufreq.temp_limit); gfx/compute
   busy accounting in amdgpu (amdgpu_fence.c, kfd) feeds it and gpu_busy_percent on the Pro.
   It replaces rmux's drivers/devfreq/ps5-gpufreq.c, which is no longer built (CONFIG_PS5_GPUFREQ=n)
 - the WGP enable check moved into gfx hw_init (it ran before the RLC was up), also on resume
   and after a GPU reset
 - 0x13dc treated as Viola like 0x13da (PCI id table, DC asic id)
 - gfx clock from SMU QueryGfxclk and the GPU temperature from Tctl instead of the CLK4 read
 - ps5_thermal dropped: its one extra sensor is temp5 (Local4) of the ps5_fan hwmon device
 - the GPU-overlay temperature (amdgpu hwmon "edge") uses #66's ps5_soc_temp() instead of its own
   copy of the same Tctl read
 - mp1: query/request gfxclk, soc temperature, WGP enable; #66's IRQ-safe mailbox locking
   (sleep entry sends with IRQs off) applied to the lock shared with ps5-cpufreq
The #66 fan fix is in ps5-fan-hwmon-curve.
